# sr-alert.env — external alert channels for the studyroadmap watchdog.
#
# WHY: during the 2026-06-01 outage nothing paged anyone (uptime-kuma was
# crashlooping). scripts/sr-alert.sh always writes /tmp/sr-DOWN + /tmp/sr-alerts.log,
# but to actually REACH you it needs at least one channel below.
#
# HOW: copy this file to sr-alert.env (same dir) and uncomment ONE line.
#   cp scripts/sr-alert.env.example scripts/sr-alert.env && edit it
# No restart needed — sr-alert.sh sources it on every alert.

# --- ntfy.sh (easiest: zero signup, install the ntfy app, pick a secret topic) ---
# NTFY_URL="https://ntfy.sh/studyroadmap-CHANGE-ME-to-a-secret-string"

# --- healthchecks.io dead-man's-switch (alerts if the watchdog STOPS pinging) ---
# Create a check, then use its /fail URL here; pair with a /ping in a healthy cron.
# HEALTHCHECK_FAIL_URL="https://hc-ping.com/your-uuid-here/fail"

# --- Slack / Discord (Discord: append /slack to the webhook URL) ---
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL="https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXX/YYY/ZZZ"

# --- Email (requires a working local MTA / `mail` command) ---
# ALERT_EMAIL="pushkersaini@gmail.com"
